.TH INVF-SWEEP 8 "2026-09" "InvariantFS" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
invf-sweep \- InvariantFS offline sweep driver (classification, transcode, seal)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B invf-sweep
.I image
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-\-fast ]
.RB [ \-\-compact ]
.RB [ \-\-seal [5\||10\||20\||25] | \-\-unseal ]
.RB [ \-\-verify\-seal ]
.RB [ \-\-stale\-mode=auto\||notify\||off ]
.RB [ \-\-heal [ \fIgroup ...\fR ] ]
.RB [ \-\-reseal\-full ]
.RB [ \-\-migrate | \-\-no\-migrate ]
.RB [ \-\-recompress ]
.RB [ \-\-realize | \-\-no\-realize ]
.br
.B invf-sweep
.I image
.RB [ \-\-redundant\-blocks
.IR f ]
.RB [ \-\-redundant\-paranoic
.IR f [: rs-vm | rs-cauchy ]]
.RB [ \-\-free\-redundant ]
.RB [ \-\-redundant\-bench ]
.br
.B invf-sweep
.I image
.BI \-\-extract\-packs " dir"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B invf-sweep
walks every live file on an unmounted InvariantFS volume and drives it
through the storage pipeline: content classification, cross-file PPMd text
batching, binary ZSTD+BCJ batching, container decomposition (ZIP/TAR/GZ and
container codecpacks), whole-file codec transcodes (e.g. JPEG -> lossless
JXL via the jxl codecpack), offline dedupe, and the generic per-segment
ZSTD floor. Every transform is guarded: the result is decoded back and
compared against the original bytes before anything is committed, so the
bit-exactness invariant holds by construction.
.PP
The volume must not be mounted. For mounted volumes use the daemon trigger
.RB ( "kill \-USR1"
on the
.BR invf-fuse (8)
process, or
.BR setfattr " \-n user.invfs.sweep \-v 1 /"
inside the mount); the
.BR invfs-sweep.timer (8)
systemd unit automates exactly that.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Report what would be done; commit nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-fast
Cheap pass: RAW files take only the generic per-segment recompress - no
classification, transcodes, decomposition, batching or dedupe.
.TP
.B \-\-compact
Run only the inode-area compaction pass.
.TP
.B \-\-seal [5\||10\||20\||25]
After the sweep, seal shadow parity with native per-chunk RS groups
(5/10/20/25%% redundancy steps; default from the volume policy). Each
chunk carries its own parity alongside the data (piggyback layout, footer
last), so a torn chunk heals from its neighbours without a second volume.
Note the sweep retires RAW originals, so an unsealed volume has no second
copy.
.TP
.B \-\-verify\-seal
Read-only seal scrub: report per-group parity drift, change nothing.
Exits 0 clean, 3 on drift, 1 on tool failure. No sweep runs.
.TP
.BI \-\-stale\-mode= auto\||notify\||off
What a bare run does about stale seal (parity older than the data):
.B auto
reseals (default),
.B notify
reports without resealing,
.B off
prints one line. An explicit
.B \-\-seal / \-\-unseal
always wins; unsealed volumes stay silent.
.TP
.BI \-\-heal [ \fIgroup ...\fR ]
Heal drifted seal groups explicitly (no group list = all drifted). Healing
is never automatic: drift is reported loudly and only this flag repairs it.
.TP
.B \-\-reseal\-full
Force a full parity recompute. By default only groups dirty since the
last seal are restriped, when provable; the rest are skipped.
.TP
.B \-\-migrate , \-\-no\-migrate
Run (default on) or skip the defrag relocate stage: live segments move
out of fragmented extents into consolidated ones. Skipped by
.B \-\-fast
and
.BR \-\-dry\-run .
.TP
.B \-\-recompress
Re-run the generic ZSTD floor on demand (implies
.BR \-\-migrate ,
skipped by
.B \-\-fast ).
.TP
.B \-\-unseal , \-\-free\-redundant
Drop the redundancy layer.
.TP
.BI \-\-redundant\-blocks " f"
Fraction of the volume devoted to redundancy blocks.
.TP
.BI \-\-redundant\-paranoic " f"[: rs-vm | rs-cauchy ]
Paranoid RS parity fraction and variant.
.TP
.B \-\-redundant\-bench
Benchmark the redundancy encoder.
.TP
.B \-\-realize , \-\-no\-realize
Accept the last sweep (free the savepoint that opened its window) or keep
the previous checkpoint live (blocks stay held until the next sweep).
After
.BR \-\-realize ,
.BR invf-rollback (8)
can no longer undo that sweep.
.TP
.BI \-\-extract\-packs " dir"
WP23 sweepboot helper: copy the volume's self-hosted codecpack directory
(on the volume at
.I /.invfs/codecpacks
or
.IR /usr/lib/invfs/codecpacks )
to
.IR dir ,
engine-side, with no sweep and no FUSE mount. Used by initramfs
maintenance boots.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B INVFS_PROFILE
Codec effort profile
.BR fast | balanced | dense | archive
(default
.BR balanced ).
When set, the tool logs the effective generic zstd level.
.TP
.B INVFS_ARC_BYTES , INVFS_DEC_MEM_LIMIT
Admission budgets; see
.BR invf-fuse (8).
.TP
.B INVFS_CODECPACKS , INVFS_TOOLS
Codecpack and tool search paths; see
.BR invarifs (7).
.TP
.B INVFS_MIN_GAIN_PCT
Minimum compression benefit (percent, default 0.5) before a file is
classified UNCOMPRESSIBLE.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success (including "nothing to do"); non-zero on I/O or volume errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR invf-fuse (8),
.BR invf-rollback (8),
.BR invf-verify (8),
.BR invarifs (7)
